              "latex": "10^{100}",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " — the company name ‘Google’ was an accidental misspelling of ‘googol’. A ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "googolplex",
              "marks": [
                "italic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "10^{\\text{googol}}",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". A googol is about 100 billion times greater than the number of elementary particles in the observable universe, and a googolplex is very big.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p18-q13-a",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find:",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p18-q13-a-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "$\\log_{10}\\text{googol}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$100$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}10^x&=10^{100}\\\\x&=100\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 20
          },
          {
            "id": "p18-q13-a-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "$\\log_{100}\\text{googol}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$50$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}100^x&=10^{100}\\\\10^{2x}&=10^{100}\\\\x&=50\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 28
          },
          {
            "id": "p18-q13-a-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "$\\log_{10}\\text{googolplex}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$10^{100}$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}10^x&=10^{10^{100}}\\\\x&=10^{100}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 20
          },
          {
            "id": "p18-q13-a-iv",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iv",
            "prompt": "$\\log_{100}\\text{googolplex}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$5\\times10^{99}$\n\nRewrite the base as $10^2$ and equate indices.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}100^x&=10^{10^{100}}\\\\10^{2x}&=10^{10^{100}}\\\\x&=\\frac{10^{100}}{2}\\\\x&=5\\times10^{99}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 36
          },
          {
            "id": "p18-q13-a-v",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "v",
            "prompt": "$\\log_{\\text{googol}}\\text{googol}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$1$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(10^{100})^x&=10^{100}\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 20
          },
          {
            "id": "p18-q13-a-vi",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "vi",
            "prompt": "$\\log_{\\text{googol}}\\text{googolplex}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$10^{98}$\n\nExpress both sides with base 10 and equate indices.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(10^{100})^x&=10^{10^{100}}\\\\10^{100x}&=10^{10^{100}}\\\\x&=\\frac{10^{100}}{100}\\\\x&=10^{98}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 36
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Which whole numbers does $\\log_2\\text{googol}$ lie between? Do not use log or ln.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$332$ and $333$.\n\nCompare $10^{100}$ with consecutive powers of 2.",
          "worked": "Calculate consecutive powers of 2 by repeated multiplication, without log or ln:\n$$\\begin{align*}2^{332}&\\approx8.7490\\times10^{99}\\\\2^{333}&\\approx1.7498\\times10^{100}\\end{align*}$$\nThus $2^{332}<10^{100}<2^{333}$, so $332<\\log_2\\text{googol}<333$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 37
      }
    ]
  },
